# Harness credentials — copy to harness/.env and fill in. NEVER commit harness/.env.
#
# These are the HARNESS's secrets, not the application's. They are deliberately
# not in the repo-root .env.example: that file is the application's template,
# read by the application's own settings and its own tests.
# Mixing agent-provider credentials into it would undo the separation that
# harness/ exists to draw.
#
# resolve.py loads harness/.env automatically if present. A real environment
# variable always wins, so CI and 1Password/direnv setups need no file at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DeepSeek — the `worker` tier's provider once you switch it over
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Reached through Claude Code's Anthropic-compatible path (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL +
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN), so no new client library is involved. Compatibility is
# a CLAIM TO TEST: run harness/models/probe-compat.sh deepseek before routing any
# real task, and read what it says about tool loops in particular.

# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenRouter — one endpoint, many models; the tier names which
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The same Anthropic-compatible path. Declared per project in harness.yaml:
#   providers: {openrouter: {env: {ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL: https://openrouter.ai/api,
#                                  ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN: "${OPENROUTER_API_KEY}"}}}
#   tiers: {worker: {provider: openrouter, model: qwen/qwen3-coder-plus}}
# Probe it first: harness/models/probe-compat.sh openrouter.

# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# There is deliberately no DEEPSEEK_MODEL or OPENROUTER_MODEL here. The model belongs to the TIER
# (harness/models/tiers.yaml) and is passed as `--model`, the same way it is for
# Anthropic. A model named here as well would be a second source of truth.
